    "chunk_text": "PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 01.\n\nPrice : Rs. 4.25 Postage : Rs. 4.50\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka of June 21, 2002\n\nSAVE THE NATION CONTRIBUTION(ABOLITION)ACT, No. 8 OF 2002\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Certified on 19th June, 2002 ]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n1Save the Nation Contribution (Abolition)Act, No. 8 of 2002\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 56/2001.\n\nAN ACT TO ABOLISH THE CHARGING OF SAVE THE NATIONCONTRIBUTION, UNDER THE SAVE THE NATION CONTRIBUTIONACT, NO. 5 OF 1996, FROM PERSONS TO WHOM THAT ACT APPLIES,\n\nWITH EFFECT FROM OCTOBER 1, 2001\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Save the NationContribution (Abolition) Act, No. 8 of 2002.\n\n2.Notwithstanding anything in the Save the NationContribution Act, No. 5 of 1996\u2014\n\n(a)the Save the Nation Contribution shall not be chargedand recovered from any person to whom that Actapplies, for any quarter of any year ; and\n\n(b)the employer of any person to whom that Act appliesshall not be required to deduct any amount that suchemployer is required to deduct from the emolumentspayable to such person, under section 4 of that Act,for any month,\n\ncommencing on or after October 1, 2001.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\n[Certified on 19th June 2002]\n\nSinhala text toprevail in case ofinconsistency.\n\nAbolition of thecharging of theSave the NationContribution witheffect fromOctober 1, 2001.\n\nShort title.\n\nSave the Nation Contribution (Abolition)Act, No. 8 of 20022"
