    "language": "en",
    "md5": "2d3ecdda0c60b274f50db07f7fb88551",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1899,
    "chunk_text": "3.In the exercise and discharge of the powers andfunctions under paragraphs (a), (b), (c), (d) and (e) of section2, it shall be the duty of the Competent Authority as far aspracticable, to be satisfied, that the programmes broadcast bythe Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation or the Sri LankaRupavahini Corporation as the case may be, comply with thefollowing conditions, in addition to any guidelines which theElection Commission may issue from time to time :\u2014\n\nCompetentAuthority to besatisfied ofcompliance withcertain conditions.\n\nCompetent Authority (Powers and Functions)Act, No. 3 of 20024\n\nanything which is against good taste or decency, orwhich is likely to incite a person to commit a crime,or which may lead to disorder, or be such as to offendany racial or religious susceptibilities, or to beoffensive to public feeling ;\n\n(b) that the programmes broadcast shall maintain a properlocal, regional and international balance with regardto the subject matter dealt with, and also generally tomaintain a high standard of quality ;\n\n(c) that any news presented through any such programmeshall be presented with due accuracy and impartialityand with due regard to the public interest.\n\n4.Any suit or prosecution instituted in a court of law byor against the Competent Authority for any act or omission infurtherance of the powers and functions assigned under thisAct, shall be deemed as an action instituted by or against theState.\n\n5.The Competent Authority may appoint such officersand servants as may be necessary for the implementation ofthe provisions of this Act, and any officer or servant soappointed shall be deemed to be a public officer.\n\n6.The Competent Authority and the officers and servantsappointed under section 5 of this Act, may be paid suchremuneration computed at such amount as may be determinedby the Election Commission which shall be a charge on theConsolidated Fund."
