    "chunk_text": "(a) to promote the wider acceptance of mediation andconciliation for the resolution and setllement ofcommercial disputes ;\n\n(b) to encourage parties to resolve commercial disputesby mediation and conciliation ;\n\nEsrablishmcnt of the Sri Lanka Commercial Mediation Centre.\n\nFunctions of the Centre.\n\n(i) to conduct training courses and workshops for thepurposes of discharging its functions ;\n\n(j) lo invest its unutilized moneys in such securities as may be approved by the Minister with the concurrence of the Minister in charge of the subject of Finance; and\n\n(k) to do all such other acts as may be necessary for, orconducive to, for the proper discharge of it'sfunctions.\n\n5. (I) The administration and management of the affairs Board ofof the Centre shall be vested in a Board of Management Management.\n\n(hereinafter referred to as \"the Board\") consisting of the following members appointed by the Minister: -\n\n(a) one member nominated by the Ceylon Chamber ofCommerce, incorporated by the Chamber ofCommerce Ordinance (Chapter 289) ;\n\n(b) one member nominated by the National Chamberof Commerce of Sri Lanka ;\n\n(c) one member nominated by the Federation of Chambers of Commerce and Industry of Sri Lanka;\n\n(d) one member nominated by the Ceylon NationalChamber of Industries, incorporated by the Ceylon National Chamber of Industries Act, No. 10 of 1969; and\n\n(e) one member nominated by the Minister in charge ofthe subject of Justice.\n\n(2) A member of the Board may at any time resign hisoflice by leuer in that behalf addressed to the Minister.\n\n(3) The Minister may, for reasons assigned, remove amember of the Board from oflice."
