    "chunk_text": "PUBLIC SERVICE PROVIDENT FUND(AMENDMENT) ACT, No.45 OF 1999\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n[Certified on 10th December, 1999]\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of December 10, 1999.\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 1\n\nPrice : Rs.3.50Postage : Rs. 3.50\n\n(Internet Version)\n\n1Public Service Provident Fund (Amendment)Act, No.45 of 1999\n\nShort title.\n\nAmendment ofsection 4 of theprincipalenactment.\n\n[Certified on 10th December, 1999]\n\nL.D.\u2013O.12/95.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE PUBLIC SERVICE PROVIDENT FUNDORDINANCE\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2013\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Public Service ProvidentFund (Amendment) Act, No.45 of 1999.\n\n2. Section 2 of the Public Service Provident Fund Ordinance(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cPrincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended by the insertion immediately after subsection (4) ofthat section, of the following subsection :\u2013\n\n\u201c(4A) for the purposes of this Ordinance, a person whoholds \u2013\n\n(a) the post of Sub - Station Master in the Railway Department; or.\n\n(b) a post in the Sri Lanka Police Reserve,\n\nshall be deemed to be a non-pensionable employee in theservice of the Government and the monthly allowance paid inlieu of salary to such person shall be deemed to be a monthlysalary\u201d.\n\n3. Section 4 of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows:\u2013\n\n(a) in subsection (1) of that section, by the substitution,for the words \u201c six per centum\u201d, of the words \u201ceightper centum\u201d ; and\n\n(b) in the proviso to subsection (2) of that section by thesubstitution, for the words \u201csix per centum\u201d, of thewords \u201ceight per centum\u201d. ;\n\nH-022545\n\nAmendment ofsection 2 ofChapter 434.\n\n2Public Service Provident Fund (Amendment)Act, No.45 of 1999\n\nAmendment ofsection 5 of theprincipalenactment."
