    "chunk_text": "MAWATHAGAMA DEVELOPMENT FOUNDATION(INCORPORATION) ACT, No. 13 OF 1999\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n[Certified on 4 th June, 1999]\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka of June 04, 1999\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 1\n\nPrice : Rs. 5.75Postage : Rs. 3.50\n\n(Internet Version)\n\nMawathagama Development Foundation(Incorporation) Act, No. 13 of 1999\n\n[Certified on 4th June, 1999]\n\nL.D.\u2013O.31/96.\n\nAN ACT TO INCORPORATE THE MAWATHAGAMA DEVELOPMENTFOUNDATION\n\nWHEREAS a Foundation called and known as the\u201cMawathagama Development Foundation\u201d has heretoforebeen formed in Mawathagama for the purpose of effectuallycarrying out and transacting all objects and matters connectedwith the said Foundation according to the rules agreed to byits members :\n\nAND WHEREAS the said Foundation has heretoforesucessfully carried out and transacted the several objects andmatters for which it was formed and has applied to beincorporated and it will for the public advantage to grant suchapplication :\n\nBE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows :\u2013\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the MawathagamaDevelopment Foundation (Incorporation) Act, No.13 of 1999.\n\n2. From and after the date of commencement of this Act,such and so many persons as now are members of theMawathagama Development Foundation (hereinafter referredto as the \u201cFoundation\u201d), or shall hereafter be admittedmembers of the Corporation hereby constituted shall be abody corporate (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cCorporation\u201d)with prepetual succession, under the name and style of the\u201cMawathagama Development Foundation\u201d and by that namemay sue and be sued in all courts with full power and authorityto have, and use a common seal and alter the same at itspleasure."
