    "chunk_text": "2. From and after the date of commencement of this Act,such and so many persons as now are members of theMawathagama Development Foundation (hereinafter referredto as the \u201cFoundation\u201d), or shall hereafter be admittedmembers of the Corporation hereby constituted shall be abody corporate (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cCorporation\u201d)with prepetual succession, under the name and style of the\u201cMawathagama Development Foundation\u201d and by that namemay sue and be sued in all courts with full power and authorityto have, and use a common seal and alter the same at itspleasure.\n\n(a) to improve the economic conditions of the poor ;\n\nShort title.\n\nPreamble.\n\nIncorporation ofthe MawathagamaDevelopmentFoundation.\n\nGeneral Objectsof the Corporation.\n\nH - 022545\n\n2Mawathagama Development Foundation(Incorporation) Act, No. 13 of 1999\n\n(b) to assist the people engaged in the domesticsubsistance sector and the export agricultural sector,and to improve productivity in such sectors ;\n\n(c) to undertake the management of land developmentand agricultural activities ;\n\n(d) to assist and encourage, rural small industries andthe generation of self employment ;\n\n(e) to encourage and provide incentives to the poor tobe self reliant ;\n\n(f) to contribute actively for the realization of theobjectives of the national programme called andknown as Samurdhi Movement for alleviation ofpoverty ;\n\n(g) to enthuse the public in the malter of primary healthcare, and to provide advise thereon ;\n\n(h) to improve health and nutrition levels, through socialactivation projects and to provide assistance forsocial welfare activities ;\n\n(i) to provide financial assistance and advice, for thesupply of drinking water ;\n\n(j) to provide advice and assistance to low income ruralpoor, in matters relating to housing ;\n\n(k) to educate the public on the ill-effects of liquor, drugsand smoking, and to free people from addictionthereto ;\n\n(l) to implement programmes for the protection of thebasic values of indigenous culture ;"
