    "chunk_size_bytes": 1773,
    "chunk_text": "(i) to disseminate knowledge and information onimproved methods of agriculture , horticultureaquaculture, sericulture, animal husbandry, freshwater fisheries and bee keeping, through thepublication and distribution of books andpamphlets and the conduct of seminars, workshops,lectures and film shows;\n\n(j) to promote thrift among the under privileged.\n\nGeneral powersof theCorporation.\n\n3Pasyodunrata Development Foundation(Incorporation) Act, No.5 of 1999\n\n5. (1) The affairs of the Corporation shall, subject to therule inforce for the time being of the Corporation, beadministered by a Board of Management consisting of theoffice-bearers and such other persons as may be provided forin such rules and elected in accordance therewith.(2) The first Board of Management of the Corporationshall be the Board of Management of the Foundation holdingoffice on the day prior to the date of commencement of thisAct.\n\n6.(1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from time totime, at any general meeting of the members and by majorityof the votes, of not less than two-thirds of the members presentand voting to make rules not inconsistent with the provisionsof this Act, or any other written law for the admission,withdrawal, resignation, retirement or expulsion of members,for the election of the office-bearers of the Board ofManagement and for the conduct of the duties of the Board ofManagement and of the various officers, agents and servantsof the Corporation by the Board of Management for theprocedure to be followed in the transaction of business, andotherwise generally, for the management of the affairs of theCorporation and the accomplishment of its objects. Such ruleswhen made may, at a like meeting and in like manner, be altered, added to, amended or rescinded."
  },
